{
  "id": "m64l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Matrices como listas de listas",
    "en": "Matrices as lists of lists"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Tablas de números"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una matriz se representa como una **lista de listas** (cada lista es una fila). Se accede con `m[fila][columna]`. `zip(*m)` es el truco para **transponer** (intercambiar filas por columnas)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "m = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]",
          "print(m[1][2])",
          "print([list(f) for f in zip(*m)])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "6",
          "[[1, 4], [2, 5], [3, 6]]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Para matemática seria de matrices se usa NumPy, pero entender la versión con listas es la base."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Tables of numbers"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A matrix is represented as a **list of lists** (each list is a row). Access it with `m[row][column]`. `zip(*m)` is the trick to **transpose** (swap rows for columns)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "m = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]",
          "print(m[1][2])",
          "print([list(f) for f in zip(*m)])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "6",
          "[[1, 4], [2, 5], [3, 6]]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "For serious matrix math use NumPy, but understanding the list version is the foundation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m64l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `transponer(m)` que devuelva la matriz transpuesta (filas <-> columnas).",
        "en": "Define `transponer(m)` returning the transposed matrix (rows <-> columns)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def transponer(m):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def transponer(m):",
        "    return [list(f) for f in zip(*m)]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "zip(*m) transpone; conviértelo a listas."
        ],
        "en": [
          "zip(*m) transposes; convert to lists."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "transponer",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [
                    1,
                    2,
                    3
                  ],
                  [
                    4,
                    5,
                    6
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                [
                  1,
                  4
                ],
                [
                  2,
                  5
                ],
                [
                  3,
                  6
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [
                    1,
                    2
                  ],
                  [
                    3,
                    4
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                [
                  1,
                  3
                ],
                [
                  2,
                  4
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m64l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `suma_matrices(a, b)` que sume dos matrices del mismo tamaño elemento a elemento.",
        "en": "Define `suma_matrices(a, b)` adding two same-size matrices element by element."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def suma_matrices(a, b):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def suma_matrices(a, b):",
        "    return [[a[i][j] + b[i][j] for j in range(len(a[i]))] for i in range(len(a))]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Recorre filas y columnas sumando a[i][j] + b[i][j]."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Iterate rows and columns adding a[i][j] + b[i][j]."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "suma_matrices",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [
                    1,
                    2
                  ],
                  [
                    3,
                    4
                  ]
                ],
                [
                  [
                    5,
                    6
                  ],
                  [
                    7,
                    8
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                [
                  6,
                  8
                ],
                [
                  10,
                  12
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [
                    1
                  ]
                ],
                [
                  [
                    9
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                [
                  10
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}